    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.03_embedded_engine_functors.sections.01_embedded_engine_functor.concrete_anchor.source_obj" ;
    silm:hasExample "In 'SourceObject', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, X is the source federation object — concretely VetRecord_Mittens in the Mittens example. It is the domain of the functor input morphism.." ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The VetRecord_Mittens_SourceObject is X is the source federation object — concretely VetRecord_Mittens in the Mittens example. It is the domain of the functor input morphism. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'X (source federation object)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_03_embedded_engine_functors_sections_01_embedded_engine_functor_concrete_anchor_functor_node
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.03_embedded_engine_functors.sections.01_embedded_engine_functor.concrete_anchor.functor_node" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The EmbeddedEngineFunctorFunctorNode is F is the EmbeddedEngineFunctor functor — it maps typed federation objects and morphisms from the source category to the target category, preserving composition and identity. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'F (the EmbeddedEngineFunctor functor)', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_03_embedded_engine_functors_sections_01_embedded_engine_functor_concrete_anchor_mapped_obj
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.03_embedded_engine_functors.sections.01_embedded_engine_functor.concrete_anchor.mapped_obj" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The MappedMittensObject is F(X) is the mapped target object — the image of VetRecord_Mittens under the functor. In the embedded engine context, F(VetRecord_Mittens) is the engine's internal representation of the vet record with the aboutness arrow preserved." .

