    silm:hasExample "In 'Replica1ForColimit', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, R_1 is the morning vet-visit replica for Mittens — contains the vaccination record and morning weight. It contributes via mu_1 to R_vee and via nu_1 to VetCarePlan_77.." ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The MorningReadingReplica is R_1 is the morning vet-visit replica for Mittens — contains the vaccination record and morning weight. It contributes via mu_1 to R_vee and via nu_1 to VetCarePlan_77. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'R_1', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .

silm:instances_papers_03_silmaril_federation_chapters_06_crdt_gossip_convergence_sections_03_gossip_colimit_diagram_concrete_anchor_r_vee
    a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.03_silmaril_federation.chapters.06_crdt_gossip_convergence.sections.03_gossip_colimit_diagram.concrete_anchor.r_vee" ;
    silm:hasLongDescription "The FullyConvergedVetRecordForMittens is R_vee is the fully converged vet record state for Mittens — contains all health readings (morning weight, afternoon temperature, evening microchip scan) from all replicas. This is the colimit colim D_gossip. Every other compatible aggregation of R_1 and R_2 must factor through R_vee via the unique mediating arrow u." .

